    {
      "title": "Cuff",
      "slug": "cuff",
      "displayOrder": 30,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 362,
        "lessonOrder": 30
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/cuff1.png\">\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/cuff2.png\">\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/cuff4.png\">\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/cuff3.png\">\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5228,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "So many options for creating the cuff of your mittens!<br>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Use your ribber. 1x1, 2x2, 2x1 ... the sky's the limit!</li>\r\n<li>Hand knit some ribbing and hang the stitches on the machine</li>\r\n<li>No Ribber?\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Reform stitches to create ribbing</li>\r\n<li>Work Mock Ribbing</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5229,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151858377",
              "title": "No ribber needed",
              "legacySlot": 1,
              "legacyComponentId": 5230,
              "order": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859815",
              "title": "Explore more Mock Ribbing",
              "legacySlot": 2,
              "legacyComponentId": 5230,
              "order": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859822",
              "title": "2 Color Pretend Ribbing",
              "legacySlot": 3,
              "legacyComponentId": 5230,
              "order": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151858398",
              "title": "Get fancy with a cabled rib",
              "legacySlot": 4,
              "legacyComponentId": 5230,
              "order": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151858391",
              "title": "Basic Ribbing without a Ribber",
              "legacyComponentId": 5231,
              "order": 4
            }
          ],
          "title": "Cuff Options",
          "slug": "cuff-options",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3630,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "A favorite cuff finish is to combine a rolled edge with ribbing. Not only is this method practical, you don't have to bother with a ribbing cast on.<br>\r\n<ol class=\"instruction-list\">\r\n<li>Use a stretchy method to cast on</lI>\r\n<li>Knit a few rows</li>\r\n<li>Transfer stitches to the ribber</li>\r\n<li>Knit the cuff <em><small>No ribber? Reform the stitches by hand</small></em></li>\r\n<li>Transfer the stitches to the main bed and continue knitting your mitten</li>\r\n\r\n</ol>\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/ribnroll.jpg\"><br>\r\n<b>Use a contrasting color for fun.</b>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5232,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859199",
              "title": "Ribber Cast On Comb for Single Bed Knitting",
              "legacyComponentId": 5233,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Rib 'n Roll Cuff",
          "slug": "rib-n-roll-cuff",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3631,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Hand",
      "slug": "hand",
      "displayOrder": 40,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 363,
        "lessonOrder": 40
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Think of the hand section of the mitten as a canvas.<br>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Small Fairisle Stitch patterns</li>\r\n<li>Stripes</li>\r\n<li>Stitch texture</li>\r\n<li>Embroidery</li>\r\n<li>Embellishments</li>\r\n<li>Isolated Motifs</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5234,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "migrationPending",
              "legacyType": "Pinterest",
              "notes": [
                "Legacy Pinterest embed; replace with static content or omit."
              ],
              "legacyFields": {
                "CHALLENGE_ASSIGNID": "650",
                "PINTERESTID": "3",
                "TYPEOF": "Pinterest"
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 5235,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Your Design Canvas",
          "slug": "your-design-canvas",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3632,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151857799",
              "title": "Stitch Multiples",
              "legacyComponentId": 5236,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Plan Ahead",
          "slug": "plan-ahead",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3633,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "migrationPending",
              "legacyType": "CustomButton",
              "notes": [
                "Unmapped legacy component type: CustomButton"
              ],
              "legacyFields": {
                "BUTTONTARGET": "blank",
                "CHALLENGE_ASSIGNID": "662",
                "CHALLENGE_COMPONENTID": "2173",
                "HREF": "/tools/KnititnowPaper.cfm",
                "LABLE": "Print your own Graph Paper"
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 5237,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<div class=\"lead\">Knitter's Graph Paper</Div><br>If you are planning to add a stitch pattern to your mittens, you need to use knitter's graph paper to plan your design.<br>If you are adding a single motif or an all over stitch pattern the ONLY way to position them correctly is to chart things out in advance.<br>Knitter's graph paper is designed to represent the shape of knitting stitches (which are normally wider than tall).<br><div class=\"lead\">To position a single motif on your mitten:</div>\r\n<ol class=\"instruction-list\">\r\n<li>Use the pattern instructions to mark off the hand section of your mitten (outlined in blue below). </li>\r\n<li>Determine how many stitches and rows are in the hand section.</li>\r\n<li>Sketch the position of your motif in that section</li>\r\n<li>Use the sketch to hand manipulate or embroider the motif</li>\r\n<li>Use stitch and row counts from the graph paper sketch to position the motif on your punchcard or electronic machine</li>\r\n\r\n\r\n</ol>\r\n<em><small>Don't forget that we are generally looking at the knitting from the private (wrong) side.  Position your motif accordingly</small></em>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/position_motif.jpg\">",
              "legacyComponentId": 5238,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "The ONE must-have tool you need",
          "slug": "the-one-must-have-tool-you-need",
          "order": 3,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3634,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Mitten Top",
      "slug": "mitten-top",
      "displayOrder": 85,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 364,
        "lessonOrder": 85
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/shortrow.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nTo shape the top of the mitten we will make a short row \"pocket\".  This is neat way to have a nicely curved top with no visible seam.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5239,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "263966757",
              "title": "Watch as we knit a sample",
              "legacyComponentId": 5240,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Short Rowed Mitten Top",
          "slug": "short-rowed-mitten-top",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3635,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "251895484",
              "title": "ShortRow Refresher",
              "legacySlot": 1,
              "legacyComponentId": 5241,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151857333",
              "title": "Automatic Wrap vs. Manual Wrap",
              "legacySlot": 2,
              "legacyComponentId": 5241,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Short Row Review",
          "slug": "short-row-review",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3636,
            "blockType": "VimeoMultiple"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Fingerless mittens are a fun and fashionable way to show off your knitting!<br>\r\nThey are fast to knit and offer the opportunity to play with color and texture without a lot of fuss.\r\n<img class=\"thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/fingerless_overview.gif\"><br><img class=\"thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/mitten_main.jpg\"><br><ul>\r\n<li>To use your pattern for a fingerless mitten, simply stop knitting the hand before the top shaping begins and stop shaping the thumb 1/2\" - 1\" less rows.</li>\r\n<li>You can choose to add ribbing to the openings, or bind off and just let the knitting roll.</li>\r\n<li>Adjust the length as you like.  Notice that some of the examples below have even left off the thumb completely.</li></ul>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <b>It's your turn ... get creative!</b><br>",
              "legacyComponentId": 5242,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "migrationPending",
              "legacyType": "Pinterest",
              "notes": [
                "Legacy Pinterest embed; replace with static content or omit."
              ],
              "legacyFields": {
                "CHALLENGE_ASSIGNID": "615",
                "CHALLENGE_COMPONENTID": "2178",
                "PINTERESTID": "14"
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 5243,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Fingerless Options",
          "slug": "fingerless-options",
          "order": 3,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3637,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\r\n\r\nAnother option for the fingertips of your mitten is to shape with decreases instead of short row shaping. <br><ol class=\"instruction-list\">\r\n<li>Scrap off 1/2 of the stitches (or put them in hold)</li>\r\n<li>TIP: Increase 1 stitch on each edge for a seaming stitch</li>\r\n<li>Work the top sections separately</li>\r\n<li>Decrease every row for about 1\" <a data-vimeoid=\"359283792\" class=\"videopopup\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>  Use a full-fashioned decrease</a></li>\r\n<li>Scrap off each section</li>\r\n<li><a data-popupcontentid=\"783\" class=\"contentpopup\"> Kitchener stitch</a> the live stitches</li>\r\n<li>Seam the decreased edges and the mitten seam with <a data-vimeoid=\"359287929\" class=\"videopopup\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>  Mattress Stitch</a></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/22/Decreased_top.jpg\">\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5447,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "imageGallery",
              "slides": [
                {
                  "src": "/v2/22/flipbook1.jpg",
                  "caption": "Work each side of the \"J\" section separately."
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/22/flipbook2.jpg",
                  "caption": "Adding a seaming stitch on each edge will prevent a \"dimple\" when the sections are seamed<br><br>\r\nWe used a \r\n<a data-vimeoid=\"359283792\" class=\"videopopup\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> 2-prong, full-fashioned decorative decrease</a>"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/22/flipbook3.jpg",
                  "caption": "<a data-popupcontentid=\"783\" class=\"contentpopup\"><i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Kitchener join</a> the live stitches"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/22/flipbook4.jpg",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/22/flipbook5.jpg",
                  "caption": "Neatly <a data-vimeoid=\"359287929\" class=\"videopopup\"> <i class=\"fa fa-youtube-play\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Mattress Stitch</a> the seams to finish"
                },
                {
                  "src": "/v2/22/flipbook6.jpg",
                  "caption": null
                }
              ],
              "legacy": {
                "enableAudio": "0",
                "playAudio": "1"
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 5448,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Decreased Mitten Top",
          "slug": "decreased-mitten-top",
          "order": 4,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3692,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<img width =\"300\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/gathered_top.jpg\"><br>\r\n<h3>In a hurry?  Want a really fast project?</h3><br>\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_gathered_top1.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\nOne of the pattern options is to simply gather the fingertips of the mitten. Watch some finishing tips for this option in the video below",
