      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "\r\n<div class=\"col-12-xs\">After the hand of the mitten is finished, the gored thumb is attached to the mitten as you knit the thumb. Using short rows we can shape and sew-as-you go for a neat, fast and good fitting thumb.<br><b>Read your pattern instructions through completely before starting to knit your thumb</b>\r\n\r\n<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_thumb.jpg\"></div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-12-xs\"><img class=\"img-thumbnail\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/mitten_magic/mitten1.jpg\"></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5244,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859000",
              "title": "Mitten Gore Thumb",
              "legacyComponentId": 5245,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Gored thumb",
          "slug": "gored-thumb",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3638,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<div>\r\nA Slotted or Peasant Thumb is another option for mittens.  <br><i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i>Add a slotted thumb to any of the mitten patterns in this collection, by adding the slotted instructions \"P\" at the red marker position in the pattern.  In other words mix 'n match tops and thumbs.\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>It may be easier for you to knit (no short row pickup as the gored thumb)</li>\r\n<li>It creates a right and left mitten</li>\r\n<li>Good when knitting in pattern</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/peasant_thumb.jpg\">\r\n</div\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5440,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "358494664",
              "title": "Slotted Thumb",
              "legacyComponentId": 5438,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Slotted Thumb",
          "slug": "slotted-thumb",
          "order": 3,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3688,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Finishing",
      "slug": "finishing",
      "displayOrder": 99,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 366,
        "lessonOrder": 99
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151857723",
              "title": "Seaming Ribbing - Plan Ahead!",
              "legacyComponentId": 5247,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Seaming Ribbing - Plan Ahead",
          "slug": "seaming-ribbing-plan-ahead",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3639,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o fa-2x\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Many knitters will graft stitches by rehanging them on the machine.  This makes it easier to stitch and easier to control the size of the stitches, making for an invisible seam.\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5248,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151849234",
              "title": "Grafting on the Machine - Knit Side",
              "legacySlot": 1,
              "legacyComponentId": 5249,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151850342",
              "title": "Grafting on the Machine - Purl Side",
              "legacySlot": 2,
              "legacyComponentId": 5249,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<blockquote class=\"smallblock\"><em>TIP: Use a contrasting color yarn for the seaming.</em></blockquote>\r\n\r\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh fa-spin fa-2x fa-fw\"></i><h3> Practice 1:Graft from the Purl Side</h3><br>\r\n\r\n<ol class=\"instruction-list\">\r\n<li>Knit 2 swatches and scrap off</li>\r\n<li>If you like, steam the swatches to tame the curl</li>\r\n<li>With the knit side facing, hang the first swatch on the machine</li>\r\n<li>With the purl side facing, hang the second swatch on the machine (the knit sides will be sandwiched together</li>\r\n<li>Follow the video instruction, graft the 2 pieces together, keeping an even tension on the stitches .. mimicking  the size and shape of the knitted stitches</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<br> <i class=\"fa fa-refresh fa-spin fa-2x fa-fw\"></i> <h3>Practice 2: Graft from the Knit Side </h3><em><small>(reverse of the previous exercise)</small></em><br><ol class=\"instruction-list\">\r\n<li>Knit 2 swatches and scrap off</li>\r\n<li>If you like, steam the swatches to tame the curl</li>\r\n<li>With the purl side facing, hang the first swatch on the machine</li>\r\n<li>With the knit side facing, hang the second swatch on the machine (the purlsides will be sandwiched together</li>\r\n<li>Follow the video instruction, graft the 2 pieces together, keeping an even tension on the stitches .. mimicking  the size and shape of the knitted stitches</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5250,
              "order": 3
            }
          ],
          "title": "Kitchner Stitch (Grafting Stitches)",
          "slug": "kitchner-stitch-grafting-stitches",
          "order": 4,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3640,
            "blockType": "Video"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Mittens in the Round",
      "slug": "mittens-in-the-round",
      "displayOrder": 101,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 374,
        "lessonOrder": 101
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Is it possible to knit mittens in the round?  YES!  But ... The gore style mitten may not be the best choice.<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Picture this:</b>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"li_7px\">\r\n<li>Ribbing can't be knit in the round. But you could cast on with waste yarn and add ribbing by hand later</li>\r\n<li>You start at the wrist and knit in the round to the thumb opening (see videos below)</li>\r\n<li>Switch to \"U\" Knitting to leave the thumb opening</li>\r\n<li>Change back to circular knitting to work the hand</li>\r\n<li>Scrap off the ribber stitches and drop the ribber</li>\r\n<li>Work the Short row top on the main bed only</li>\r\n<li><b>The challenge</b>:  How to pick up and knit the thumb?\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Slip the mitten between the beds and hang both edges of the gore opening on the main bed needles, then transfer half to the ribber and knit the thumb in the round</li>\r\n<li>Knit the thumb separately, either flat or in the round and sew it to the mitten opening</ll>\r\n<li>Hand knit the thumb in the round</li>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/circular_mitten.jpg\">\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5436,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151858632",
              "title": "Circular (tubular) Knitting with the Ribber",
              "legacySlot": 1,
              "legacyComponentId": 5437,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859462",
              "title": "Half Circular U-Knitting",
              "legacySlot": 2,
              "legacyComponentId": 5437,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "358379693",
              "title": "Provisional Knitting for a Slotted Thumb",
              "legacySlot": 3,
              "legacyComponentId": 5437,
              "order": 2
            }
          ],
          "title": "Seamless Possibilities",
          "slug": "seamless-possibilities",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3687,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Trigger Mittens",
      "slug": "trigger-mittens",
      "displayOrder": 106,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 376,
        "lessonOrder": 106
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n    mark {\r\n        background-color: #F8DEEC;\r\n        color: black;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n        Trigger mittens (AKA Glittens) can easily be created from our basic Mitten Collection patterns.<br>Because everyone's hand is shaped a bit differently, it's best to custom position the finger for your mitten.\r\n  <div class=\"table-responsive\">\r\n     <table class=\"table table-striped\">\r\n         <tbody class=\"small\">\r\n             <tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">1</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>Determine the length of \"Q\": Multiply it by your row gauge  _______________</td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n\r\n <tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">2</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>Determine the length of \"M\": Multiply it by your row gauge _______________</td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n\r\n <tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">3</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>Determine the desired finger circumference \"C\": Multiply it by your stitch gauge  _______________</td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">4</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>After placing the red markers in the pattern, Knit for \"Q\" rows</td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">5</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>At each side of the knitting, scrap off 1/2 of \"C\" stitches</td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">6</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>Continue knitting the mitten as instructed</td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">7</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>Seam the lower part of the mitten and thumb</td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">7</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>Pick up the \"T\" stitches to form the finger. <B>Add a seaming stitch at each side</b></td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">8</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>Knit the finger for \"M\" rows</td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">9</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>Gather the finger tip as instructed for the thumb</td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n                 <td>\r\n                     <span class=\"fa-stack\">\r\n                         <span class=\"fa fa-square-o fa-stack-2x\"></span>\r\n                         <strong class=\"fa-stack-1x\">\r\n                             <p class=\"text-muted small\">9</p>\r\n                         </strong>\r\n                     </span>\r\n                 </td>\r\n                 <td>Seam the mitten and work in all ends</td>\r\n             </tr>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n     </table>\r\n\r\n </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n       \r\n        <img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/Trigger_mitten2.jpg\">\r\n    \r\n\r\n<img class=\"zoom\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/56/trigger_mitten01.jpg\">\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 5453,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Custom Fit Glitten Instructions",
          "slug": "custom-fit-glitten-instructions",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 3695,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
